<% content_for :title, "Terms of sale | #{current_store.name}" %>
<%= render layout: "pages/legal", locals: { eyebrow: "Legal", title: "Terms of sale" } do %>
  <h2>1. Who you are buying from</h2>
  <p>These terms govern every order placed on this store, operated by
     <b><%= current_store.name %></b> (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;).
     <mark class="legal__todo">Add your registered company name, business number and registered address here.</mark>
     Placing an order means you accept these terms as they read on the day of your order.</p>

  <h2>2. The product</h2>
  <p>We sell a food supplement. It is not a medicine and it does not treat, prevent or cure any
     condition. It is not intended for anyone under 18, for pregnant or breastfeeding women, or for
     anyone under medical supervision without advice from their doctor. Do not exceed the stated
     daily serving. Photography is illustrative; packaging may change.</p>

  <h2>3. Prices and payment</h2>
  <p>Prices are shown in <%= current_store.currency.to_s.upcase %> and include applicable taxes unless
     stated otherwise at checkout. Shipping, where charged, is shown before you confirm. Payment is
     taken at the moment you confirm your order, by card through Stripe or through PayPal. We never
     see or store your full card number.</p>
  <p>A price shown in error does not bind us. If we discover an error before dispatch we will contact
     you and you may confirm at the corrected price or cancel for a full refund.</p>

  <h2>4. Your order</h2>
  <p>Your order is an offer to buy. The contract is formed when we send you the confirmation email.
     We may refuse an order — for example where stock has run out, where we cannot ship to your
     address, or where we suspect fraud — and will refund you in full if we do.</p>

  <h2>5. Delivery</h2>
  <p>See our <%= link_to "shipping policy", shipping_policy_path %> for destinations, times and costs.
     Risk passes to you on delivery.</p>

  <h2>6. Cancelling and returning</h2>
  <p>See our <%= link_to "refund policy", refunds_path %>. Nothing in these terms limits the statutory
     rights you have as a consumer.</p>

  <h2>7. Our liability</h2>
  <p>We are liable for foreseeable loss caused by our breach of these terms. We are not liable for
     business losses, nor for loss we could not have foreseen. Nothing here excludes liability for
     death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot
     lawfully be excluded.</p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may change these terms. The version that applies to your order is the one published when you
     ordered.</p>

  <h2>9. Law and disputes</h2>
  <p><mark class="legal__todo">State the governing law and the courts that have jurisdiction — normally
     the country where your company is registered.</mark> If something goes wrong, write to
     <%= mail_to current_store.support_email %> first: most problems are settled in a day.</p>
<% end %>
